1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,200
It's time to change seats.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:07,380
<i>This one seat change</i>

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:10,360
<i>flipped my mundane high school life</i>

4
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:12,640
<i>right upside down.</i>
[I like you.]

5
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:13,970
Huh?

6
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:16,270
<i>Is he...</i>

7
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:18,240
<i>pranking me?</i>

8
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:22,540
<i>Hold on.</i>

9
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:25,520
<i>What if that note...</i>

10
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:27,820
<i>wasn't a prank?</i>

11
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,660
Ms. Komori?

12
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:33,250
<i>Does that mean I got in his way?</i>

13
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:35,640
<i>He's got the brains and the looks.</i>

14
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:38,030
<i>He's the highest tier guy in our school.</i>

15
00:00:38,030 --> 00:00:42,510
<i>If I actually did piss him off,
my high school career is over.</i>

16
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:44,680
What are you doing?

17
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:47,020
It's the real deal.

18
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:49,030
That note was for you.

19
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:51,670
What?

20
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:53,670
If you want to know why I like you...

21
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:56,980
Well, you'll find out.

22
00:00:56,980 --> 00:00:58,060
[Your bed hair, your hunched back]
[You never prioritize yourself]

23
00:00:58,060 --> 00:01:01,490
Keep pointing out my bad traits.

24
00:01:01,490 --> 00:01:02,840
I wasn't pointing out anything bad.

25
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:05,590
These are stuff I like about you.

26
00:01:05,590 --> 00:01:08,830
<i>You prioritize others,
even at your own expense.</i>

27
00:01:08,830 --> 00:01:11,400
Because you're kind.

28
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:22,900
Cheers to us.

29
00:02:04,590 --> 00:02:08,510
[Adapted from Mashiroito's work of the same title]

30
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:23,840
Asamiya?

31
00:02:35,150 --> 00:02:38,950
You said you liked me, but...

32
00:02:45,340 --> 00:02:48,900
You meant as friends, right?

33
00:02:52,250 --> 00:02:54,280
What do you think?

34
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:11,320
<i>What sort of dream was that?</i>

35
00:03:29,610 --> 00:03:30,950
[Your bed hair, your hunched back]
[You never prioritize yourself]

36
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:32,900
<i>These are stuff</i>

37
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:35,950
<i>I like about you.</i>

38
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:44,740
<i>Asamiya has since been relentless
with the sticky notes.</i>

39
00:03:45,790 --> 00:03:49,570
<i>At the pace he's going,</i>

40
00:03:49,570 --> 00:03:53,750
<i>he might fill an entire notebook
by the end of this semester.</i>

41
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:06,710
Something good happen?

42
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:11,280
You don't normally wake up so early.

43
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:13,600
It's just one of those days.

44
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:16,950
See you later.

45
00:04:16,950 --> 00:04:19,070
Wait.

46
00:04:19,070 --> 00:04:20,380
You've got some hair sticking up.

47
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:22,590
I know.

48
00:04:22,590 --> 00:04:24,170
Just leave it.

49
00:04:24,170 --> 00:04:25,540
Huh?

50
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:27,730
See you.

51
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:49,080
Morning.

52
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:51,600
Morning.

53
00:04:53,330 --> 00:04:56,810
You kept your bed hair intact.

54
00:04:56,810 --> 00:05:01,330
You said you wanted to touch it
once every three days.

55
00:05:01,330 --> 00:05:03,740
If I had it my way, it'd be every day.

56
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,590
What's in the bag?

57
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:11,270
Just a small gift. Here.

58
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:13,730
Bread?

59
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:17,670
To make up for the one you got me.

60
00:05:17,670 --> 00:05:20,500
It's only the store-bought stuff, though.

61
00:05:24,550 --> 00:05:26,450
Asamiya?

62
00:05:29,730 --> 00:05:33,170
When I die, put this in the coffin with me.

63
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:36,540
Just eat it. Bread doesn't last that long.

64
00:05:38,090 --> 00:05:41,050
Fine. Thanks.

65
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:50,800
Also, feel free to pass me less notes.

66
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:53,650
I'm sure writing all that is a hassle.

67
00:05:53,650 --> 00:05:56,040
I was already keeping myself in check.

68
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,120
Seriously?

69
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,730
Yeah, I still have lots more to say.

70
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:05,680
But if you want, I'll slow down the pace.

71
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:08,390
Thanks.

72
00:06:10,130 --> 00:06:13,250
<i>Asamiya's a kind guy.</i>

73
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:17,550
<i>I enjoy hanging out with him.</i>

74
00:06:17,550 --> 00:06:19,300
<i>But there's one catch.</i>

75
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:23,520
<i>Something I didn't realize</i>

76
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:27,740
<i>until I'd become friends with him.</i>

77
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:30,090
'Sup!

78
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:34,000
You came to school with someone?

79
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,420
Yeah.

80
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:41,470
<i>Becoming friends with Asamiya</i>

81
00:06:41,470 --> 00:06:45,850
<i>means interacting with his posse.</i>

82
00:06:45,850 --> 00:06:47,710
- Did you do the homework?
- No.

83
00:06:47,710 --> 00:06:49,710
Didn't think so.

84
00:06:49,710 --> 00:06:51,930
Yeah, you made that obvious enough.

85
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:55,270
Let me copy yours? Please?

86
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:03,290
Sakaki, you broke up with another girl?

87
00:07:03,290 --> 00:07:05,030
Yeah. It didn't work out.

88
00:07:05,030 --> 00:07:06,790
Dude.

89
00:07:06,790 --> 00:07:09,340
How long did your longest relationship last?

90
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:11,510
Uh...

91
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:15,350
Two or three...

92
00:07:15,350 --> 00:07:16,680
Months?

93
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,180
Weeks.

94
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,250
Bingo.

95
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:21,760
<i>Their conversation sounds foreign to me.</i>

96
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:25,510
So, Asamiya. Anyone on your mind?

97
00:07:25,510 --> 00:07:27,150
Yeah.

98
00:07:27,150 --> 00:07:29,010
Seriously?

99
00:07:29,010 --> 00:07:30,930
- Who's the lucky girl?
- Yeah, I'm curious.

100
00:07:30,930 --> 00:07:33,290
- Asamiya's into someone?
- What a shocker.

101
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:34,960
Let's leave it at that.

102
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:39,300
Have you found someone new, Sakaki?

103
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:42,860
Not really.

104
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:46,120
Hey, I could go for Mayama.

105
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,230
Huh?

106
00:07:47,230 --> 00:07:50,440
It's fine, I swing both ways.

107
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:53,430
No, um...

108
00:07:53,430 --> 00:07:55,590
Sorry, he's off-limits.

109
00:07:55,590 --> 00:07:59,350
Dude, I was joking.

110
00:07:59,350 --> 00:08:00,790
Yeah, obviously.

111
00:08:00,790 --> 00:08:03,540
But if your preferences were flexible,

112
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:06,300
who'd you pick from this class?

113
00:08:20,510 --> 00:08:21,730
Something up?

114
00:08:21,730 --> 00:08:23,550
No.

115
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:28,150
Do you work out?

116
00:08:28,150 --> 00:08:31,640
Nah. I sometimes run to the station, though.

117
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:33,290
That's impressive.

118
00:08:33,290 --> 00:08:36,670
I'm practically a noodle over here.

119
00:08:37,650 --> 00:08:39,660
I like you, noodle body and all.

120
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:43,060
Uh, thanks?

121
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:44,810
Wait.

122
00:08:47,590 --> 00:08:50,240
Can you wear your jacket?

123
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,630
Huh?

124
00:08:51,630 --> 00:08:53,880
But we're running laps today.

125
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:55,610
That's exactly why I'm asking.

126
00:08:57,130 --> 00:09:00,810
Sweat makes your shirt go sheer.

127
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:05,120
I didn't bring my track jacket today.

128
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:11,030
Here, wear mine.

129
00:09:11,030 --> 00:09:13,830
Don't let the other guys see your skin.

130
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:18,800
Who'd get worked up seeing that?

131
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:20,400
Me.

132
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:24,090
See you in the gymnasium.

133
00:09:42,350 --> 00:09:45,230
<i>Smells like Asamiya.</i>

134
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:49,620
<i>No. Weird thoughts, begone!</i>

135
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:54,370
One, two, three, four.

136
00:09:54,370 --> 00:09:58,310
Five, six, seven, eight.

137
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:04,180
<i>Asamiya's definition of "liking" someone</i>

138
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:09,170
<i>isn't anything serious, right?</i>

139
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:13,010
<i>His posse certainly acts like
it'd be something casual.</i>

140
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:16,830
Now pair up and stretch.

141
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:19,020
Yes, sir.

142
00:10:20,810 --> 00:10:24,220
Uh...

143
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:33,850
Are you flexible?

144
00:10:33,850 --> 00:10:37,420
Not at all.

145
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:39,320
Then I'll go easy on you.

146
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:41,090
Thanks.

147
00:10:44,930 --> 00:10:46,360
Ow, ouch!

148
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:49,670
What happened to going easy on me?

149
00:10:49,670 --> 00:10:52,520
Seriously, quit pushing!

150
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,250
No.

151
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:57,660
You're going to break something!

152
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:59,220
I'm gonna rip in half!

153
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:02,080
Let's test your limits.

154
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:05,630
Hey, quit it! Ow!

155
00:11:05,630 --> 00:11:07,670
And swap.

156
00:11:08,330 --> 00:11:10,910
Too bad.

157
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:23,830
Here I go.

158
00:11:23,830 --> 00:11:25,280
Sure.

159
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:30,590
Are you even trying?

160
00:11:30,590 --> 00:11:32,580
I'm giving it all I got.

161
00:11:35,140 --> 00:11:37,990
Ever heard the phrase, "poetic justice"?

162
00:11:37,990 --> 00:11:39,400
Huh?

163
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:43,560
Hey, pause. Seriously.

164
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:47,200
This is payback.

165
00:11:53,530 --> 00:11:55,310
My bad.

166
00:12:05,590 --> 00:12:07,220
Huh?

167
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:10,640
Yo, quit flirting over there.

168
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:14,910
Killjoys.

169
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:33,260
Shouldn't you run at your own pace?

170
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:35,310
I am running.

171
00:12:35,310 --> 00:12:37,210
No, I mean...

172
00:12:37,210 --> 00:12:38,700
Asamiya!

173
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:41,230
I know you can go faster! Pick it up!

174
00:12:41,230 --> 00:12:42,700
See?

175
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:47,610
Wait for me. I'll see you in a lap.

176
00:12:58,910 --> 00:13:02,850
Mayama, you've become best buds with Asamiya.

177
00:13:02,850 --> 00:13:05,540
- You think?
- Yeah, you haven't noticed?

178
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:08,510
He spends more time with you than us now.

179
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:13,580
Give it to me straight.
What do you think of him?

180
00:13:13,580 --> 00:13:15,710
Well...

181
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:23,600
I don't know.

182
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:25,880
I guess he feels far away?

183
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:29,820
Far away, huh?

184
00:13:46,850 --> 00:13:50,090
- I'm beat...
- Mayama.

185
00:13:50,090 --> 00:13:52,000
Asamiya's calling for you.

186
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,340
Huh?

187
00:13:58,110 --> 00:14:00,570
Hey.

188
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:02,890
'Sup.

189
00:14:02,890 --> 00:14:05,890
Sorry, did I do something wrong?

190
00:14:05,890 --> 00:14:08,440
You were seriously miffed earlier.

191
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,470
Miffed?

192
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:14,040
I guess so.

193
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:16,150
I told you to wait.

194
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,710
Huh?

195
00:14:18,710 --> 00:14:21,270
But you ran with Sakaki and Tsunekawada.

196
00:14:21,270 --> 00:14:23,130
Don't leave me in the dust next time.

197
00:14:23,130 --> 00:14:24,780
Sure.

198
00:14:25,890 --> 00:14:28,570
I guess?

199
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:30,990
Is that why you called me here?

200
00:14:30,990 --> 00:14:33,630
Huh? I thought you called me here.

201
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:37,450
Busted.

202
00:14:37,450 --> 00:14:40,180
- Hey!
- Go for it, you two.

203
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:43,840
If Asamiya feels so far, then get close!

204
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:44,840
They locked us out.

205
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:46,010
It won't last long.

206
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:48,290
You're taking this easily.

207
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:54,830
I feel far away to you?

208
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:59,760
Uh, well...

209
00:15:05,270 --> 00:15:07,120
You okay?

210
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:09,070
Yeah, the wind's just sort of chilly.

211
00:15:09,070 --> 00:15:11,250
Mayama's looking cold, Asamiya.

212
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:13,390
Why not warm him up?

213
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:19,830
It's fine. I'm used to the cold.

214
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:26,980
Huh?

215
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:35,660
It'll get them to stop.

216
00:15:38,290 --> 00:15:40,680
Do I still feel far?

217
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:53,720
Smells like you.

218
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,900
Stop, you'll cause a misunderstanding.

219
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:58,720
Yeah?

220
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,380
I mean...

221
00:16:01,110 --> 00:16:02,920
You only "like" me

222
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:07,090
as a friend, right?

223
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:09,880
Like you "like" everyone else.

224
00:16:11,350 --> 00:16:13,760
Of course not.

225
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:14,930
And cut!

226
00:16:14,930 --> 00:16:16,730
That's enough flirting for today.

227
00:16:16,730 --> 00:16:18,250
- Did you get a good shot?
- Sure did.

228
00:16:18,250 --> 00:16:20,810
This is sure to do numbers.

229
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:25,190
Upload the video, and you're dead.

230
00:16:25,190 --> 00:16:28,860
I was joking. You know I wouldn't.

231
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,810
Too bad.

232
00:16:36,810 --> 00:16:37,900
I knew it.

233
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:39,960
We'd get crazy followers, though.

234
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,710
Asamiya?

235
00:16:41,710 --> 00:16:45,000
I'm sending the video to my phone
before it's deleted.

236
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,950
Why?

237
00:16:48,350 --> 00:16:51,070
I'll delete it if you want me to.

238
00:16:51,070 --> 00:16:54,370
So long as it doesn't spread, it's fine.

239
00:16:54,370 --> 00:16:55,470
It'll be my family heirloom.

240
00:16:55,470 --> 00:16:58,470
Yeah, anything but that.

241
00:17:12,910 --> 00:17:15,150
Mayama.

242
00:17:15,150 --> 00:17:16,680
Got a moment?

243
00:17:17,250 --> 00:17:18,760
<i>Oh no.</i>

244
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:21,760
<i>Is this it?</i>

245
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:25,180
<i>Are they gonna beat me up?</i>

246
00:17:26,510 --> 00:17:31,160
<i>Are they mad I took Asamiya away from them?</i>

247
00:17:33,370 --> 00:17:35,060
Mayama.

248
00:17:39,610 --> 00:17:41,270
- We're sorry!
- We're sorry!

249
00:17:42,470 --> 00:17:43,870
Huh?

250
00:17:44,750 --> 00:17:49,360
Asamiya got seriously pissed at us
for our stunt this afternoon.

251
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:50,870
He said we took it too far.

252
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:55,630
Asamiya's not the most social guy, right?

253
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:59,230
So, it was surprising to see him trust you.

254
00:17:59,230 --> 00:18:01,690
As his only other friends,
we were happy for him.

255
00:18:01,690 --> 00:18:05,560
But we definitely spun out of control. Sorry.

256
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:07,850
You really don't have to apologize.

257
00:18:07,850 --> 00:18:10,950
Mayama, can we be friends, too?

258
00:18:10,950 --> 00:18:13,560
- Huh?
- Hang out with us.

259
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:14,990
Not just with Asamiya.

260
00:18:14,990 --> 00:18:18,120
Well, I'm not really...

261
00:18:26,670 --> 00:18:29,150
Okay. Sure.

262
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:31,710
- Awesome.
- Nice!

263
00:18:31,710 --> 00:18:34,370
So, what's our next move?

264
00:18:34,370 --> 00:18:37,000
<i>Maybe we are the same.</i>

265
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:40,840
<i>I had put a line between us.</i>

266
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:43,500
<i>But now that we're actually talking,</i>

267
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:45,950
<i>I can see Sakaki and Tsunekawada</i>

268
00:18:45,950 --> 00:18:49,390
<i>are just two normal classmates of mine.</i>

269
00:18:49,390 --> 00:18:51,440
<i>And...</i>

270
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:53,270
<i>Do I still feel far?</i>

271
00:18:53,270 --> 00:18:55,410
<i>Maybe Asamiya is, too.</i>

272
00:19:01,530 --> 00:19:03,410
Asamiya.

273
00:19:04,510 --> 00:19:07,000
Chatting without me, again?

274
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,240
It's nothing that serious.

275
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:10,910
We were talking...

276
00:19:13,530 --> 00:19:15,560
Because we're friends.

277
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:18,440
Sakaki and Tsunekawada are my friends now.

278
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:21,980
What's wrong with hanging out with them?

279
00:19:21,980 --> 00:19:26,060
I don't want you restricting who I talk to.

280
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:29,980
Sorry.

281
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:33,540
I've got an idea.

282
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:36,180
Since the culture festival is coming up,

283
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:39,410
let's all join the planning committee
for our class.

284
00:19:39,410 --> 00:19:40,600
Planning committee?

285
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:42,470
Brilliant idea.

286
00:19:42,470 --> 00:19:45,030
Want in, Asamiya?

287
00:19:46,870 --> 00:19:48,340
Sure.

288
00:19:48,340 --> 00:19:49,510
Then that's that.

289
00:19:49,510 --> 00:19:51,360
Let's start brainstorming our set-up.

290
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:52,440
What to do...

291
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,230
- Any ideas?
- The world's our oyster.

292
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:55,810
How about the classic maid cafe?

293
00:19:55,810 --> 00:19:57,060
Dude, we're all guys.

294
00:19:57,060 --> 00:19:59,810
Asamiya would look great in a maid dress.

295
00:19:59,810 --> 00:20:01,750
- I can see it.
- Hell no.

296
00:20:01,750 --> 00:20:03,300
Drop it.

297
00:20:03,300 --> 00:20:05,200
Think of something else.

298
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:12,330
You weren't put off by the idea?

299
00:20:12,330 --> 00:20:14,180
Huh?

300
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:19,140
The planning committee.
I hope we didn't force that on you.

301
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:22,050
You didn't.

302
00:20:23,350 --> 00:20:27,280
You always look out for me like that.

303
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:31,010
Making sure I'm okay with whatever.

304
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:36,440
I'd never do something
you're not okay with.

305
00:20:37,140 --> 00:20:39,940
Which reminds me, I hugged you earlier.

306
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:42,430
I'm sorry if that made you uncomfortable.

307
00:20:48,930 --> 00:20:51,650
That's exactly what I'm talking about.

308
00:20:51,650 --> 00:20:53,740
You're really kind, Asamiya.

309
00:20:56,030 --> 00:20:58,580
I take this road to the end.

310
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:00,360
See you tomorrow.

311
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:09,820
<i>Asamiya's "like" was not as a friend.</i>

312
00:21:29,250 --> 00:21:32,080
<i>Which means...</i>

313
00:21:32,080 --> 00:21:35,900
<i>I have to give him a reply eventually.</i>

314
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:41,070
<i>I don't dislike Asamiya.</i>

315
00:21:41,070 --> 00:21:45,510
<i>If anything,</i>

316
00:21:45,510 --> 00:21:47,340
<i>I'm glad he likes me.</i>

317
00:21:49,050 --> 00:21:50,910
<i>But...</i>

318
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:59,360
<i>If I had to give him a reply,</i>

319
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:01,770
<i>It wouldn't be a "yes".</i>

320
00:22:02,820 --> 00:22:05,720
I'm happy you feel that way.

321
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,340
But...

322
00:22:08,310 --> 00:22:10,340
I'm sorry.

323
00:22:10,340 --> 00:22:11,790
What are you talking about?

324
00:22:11,790 --> 00:22:13,270
Huh?

325
00:22:13,950 --> 00:22:17,170
Dude, obviously we were joking.

326
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:19,580
She'd never confess to a guy like you.

327
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:21,400
Exactly.

328
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:22,980
You thought we were serious?

329
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:26,120
Yeah, she's totally out of your league.

330
00:22:26,120 --> 00:22:28,950
I'm cracking up!

331
00:22:32,810 --> 00:22:35,150
<i>A guy like Asamiya...</i>

332
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:40,170
<i>is way out of my league.</i>

333
00:22:41,660 --> 00:22:44,400
<i>I'm sure he's only feeling confused.</i>

334
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:48,220
<i>He'll eventually realize he was wrong.</i>

335
00:24:11,980 --> 00:24:13,990
Our class will be doing

336
00:24:13,990 --> 00:24:15,790
a haunted house for the culture festival!

337
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:19,510
Is there someone who catches your eye?

338
00:24:19,510 --> 00:24:22,240
We agreed Mayama would be a werewolf.

339
00:24:22,240 --> 00:24:24,120
Cute.

340
00:24:24,120 --> 00:24:25,730
Perfect.

341
00:24:25,730 --> 00:24:27,430
Scare you?

342
00:24:27,430 --> 00:24:31,340
Why do I like him so much?

343
00:24:31,340 --> 00:24:34,010
But I'm sure about one thing.

344
00:24:34,010 --> 00:24:36,660
Mayama is my first real crush.

345
00:24:36,660 --> 00:24:40,240
Be more confident in yourself.

346
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:41,310
Here.

347
00:24:41,310 --> 00:24:43,480
- Huh?
- Perfect for the name, "Hare", right?

348
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:45,040
This one's for you.

349
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:46,710
When you confessed to me,

350
00:24:46,710 --> 00:24:49,660
I think I was happy.

351
00:24:49,660 --> 00:24:51,560
It's just...

352
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:53,120
There's better people out there for you.

353
00:24:53,120 --> 00:24:57,200
But I like 'you', Mayama.

